{:value "BOB"} "Bobsleigh"] "\n" [:option {:value "CCS"} "Cross Country Skiing"] "\n" [:option {:value "CUR"} "Curling"] "\n" [:option {:value "FSK"} "Figure Skating"] "\n" [:option {:value "IHO"} "Ice Hockey"] "\n" [:option {:value "LUG"} "Luge"] "\n" [:option {:value "NCB"} "Nordic Combined"] "\n" [:option {:value "STK"} "Short Track Speed Skating"] "\n" [:option {:value "SKN"} "Skeleton"] "\n" [:option {:value "SJP"} "Ski Jumping"] "\n" [:option {:value "SBD"} "Snowboarding"] "\n" [:option {:value "SSK"} "Speed Skating"]]] [:script {} "$('#sports_in_same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/editions/58/sports/'+$('#sports_in_same_games_select').val()})"] [:form {:id "other_games_form", :class "form-inline", :style "display: inline", :method "get"} [:select {:name "year", :id "sport_in_other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "Freestyle Skiing in other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "43"} "1988 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "44"} "1992 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "45"} "1994 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "46"} "1998 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "47"} "2002 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "49"} "2006 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "57"} "2010 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "66"} "2012 Winter Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "68"} "2016 Winter Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "60"} "2018 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "70"} "2020 Winter Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "62"} "2022 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "73"} "2024 Winter Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "72"} "2026 Winter Olympics"]]] [:script {} "$('#sport_in_other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/editions/' + $('#sport_in_other_games_select').val() + '/sports/FRS'})"] "\n" [:h1 {} "Freestyle Skiing at the 2014 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:table {:class "biodata"} "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Dates"] "\n" [:td {} "6 – 21 February 2014"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Medal Events"] "\n" [:td {} "10"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Venues"] "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/891"} "Ekstrim-Park Rosa Khutor, Krasnaya Polyana"]] "\n"] "\n"]] "\n" [:div {:class "description"} "\n" [:p {} "Freestyle skiing events were held at the " [:a {:href "/venues/891"} "Rosa Khutor Extreme Park"] " in the Mountain Cluster of venues in Krasnaya Polyana, about 60 kilometres northeast of Sochi/Adler, where the indoor events were contested at the Coastal Cluster. The entire Mountain Cluster of venues was built specifically for the 2014 Sochi Olympic Games. The freestyle skiing program was expanded by four events with halfpipe and slopestyle events for both men and women added to the standard program of moguls, aerials, and skiier-cross. Freestyle skiing in Sochi was dominated by North America, with Canada and the United States winning 7 of the 10 gold medals, and over half of all medals awarded – 16 of 30."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Freestyle skiing was marked by some tragedy leading up to the events. Prior to the Games, Brazilian freestyler " [:a {:href "/athletes/107183"} "Lais Souza"] " was training in Utah when she was tragically injured in a fall, rendering her quadriplegic after a cervical spine injury. Souza had previously competed at the Olympics in gymnastics in 2004-08 and was looking to become the first Olympics gymnast to also compete at the Winter Olympics. During the Games, Russian freestyler Mariya Komassarova was also injured training, breaking and dislocating her back. She underwent several surgeries but it was later announced that she was a paraplegic, although it is early in her recovery."] "\n\n" [:p {} "One year before Sochi, Canadian freestyle skiier Sarah Burke, who would have been a medal contender in Sochi, fell and hit her head while training. She sustained a severe head injury and died a few days later. Several of the Sochi freestylers attempted to compete with a black armband in her memory but the International Olympic Committee (IOC) would not allow this, quoting " [:em {} "Olympic Charter"] " rules against advertising, though it was hard to know what the skiiers were advertising. In Burke’s honor, the skiiers came up with something better, before the IOC knew about it. Her ashes were scattered over the halfpipe where she would have competed, leaving her memory there in perpetuity."] "\n\n" [:p {} "After all that the events seemed but an afterthought but they went off well. The snowboarders initially had complaints about the difficulty and safety of the slopestyle course, and the layout of the halfpipe. But some changes were made and no major injuries occurred during the competitions. The freestylers competed after the snowboarders, for the most part, and they had few complaints."] "\n\n"] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "Events"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n" [:thead {} "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Event"] "\n" [:th {} "Status"] "\n" [:th {} "Date"] "\n" [:th {} "Participants"] "\n" [:th {} "NOCs"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/350206"} "Moguls, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "10 February 2014"] "\n" [:td {} "29"] "\n" [:td {} "11"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/350212"} "Aerials, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "17 February 2014"] "\n" [:td {} "21"] "\n" [:td {} "9"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/350234"} "Ski Cross, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "20 February 2014"] "\n" [:td {} "31"] "\n" [:td {} "13"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/350220"} "Halfpipe, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "18 February 2014"] "\n" [:td {} "28"] "\n" [:td {} "13"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/350227"} "Slopestyle, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "13 February 2014"] "\n" [:td {} "32"] "\n" [:td {} "15"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/350256"} "Moguls, Women"]] "\n" [:td {}